<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <MemeDef>
    <defName>ARIOIAF_BloodOfTheDragon</defName>
    <label>Blood of the Dragon</label>
    <description>Followers claim descent from Valyria's dragonlords and hold their blood to be a sacred inheritance that must remain undiluted.\n\nConsenting adult blood relatives may form romantic partnerships without the usual taboo, whatever their Westerosi faith; attraction and ordinary relationship choices still apply. A follower partnered with blood kin gains +3 mood, while one partnered outside the bloodline suffers -4. Royal blood must be exalted.</description>
    <category>Normal</category><groupDef>ARIOIAF_WesterosiTraditions</groupDef><impact>2</impact><renderOrder>76</renderOrder>
    <iconPath>UI/Memes/BloodOfTheDragon</iconPath>
    <!-- Player-selectable. It used to carry hiddenInChooseMemes plus a factionWhitelist of
         ARIOIAF_Valyria, which together made it unpickable: Dialog_ChooseMemes.CanUseMeme
         rejects hidden memes outright, and then IdeoUtility.IsMemeAllowedFor rejects anything
         whose factionWhitelist excludes the player's faction def. Both had to go.

         Valyria still receives it unconditionally - it is in that faction's requiredMemes, and
         IsMemeAllowedFor returns true for a required meme before it ever reaches the whitelist
         check, so dropping the whitelist costs Valyria nothing.

         randomizationSelectionWeightFactor stays 0 on purpose: this should be a deliberate
         choice, not something a randomly generated NPC faith rolls into.

         The supplemental kin-relationship patch lets followers of this meme OR the Kept Pure
         precept use the preserved core adult-only kin romance and opinion rules, independently
         of faith structure. Royal rank and other ideology requirements remain separate. -->
    <!-- Two requirements, and the second is the one that pays for the meme.

         Royalty: exalted - dragonlords holding themselves above common men must at least exalt
         royal rank. It also satisfies Feudalism's "one of exalted/respected", so the two never
         fight - which is exactly why it is not a real cost on its own.

         Lineage: kept pure - the actual price. Both of the core assembly's dragon-blood patches
         REMOVE penalties (full romance chance between kin, and the incest opinion hit stripped),
         so without this the meme was 2 impact of pure upside. This turns "you may marry kin"
         into "you are expected to": marrying outside the bloodline now carries a standing mood
         penalty, so pairing colonists off becomes a decision with a cost.

         Rightful rule and disapproval of other faiths stay suggested rather than forced
         (associatedMemes in Ideology/Patches/MemeAssociations.xml), so the meme remains a
         tradition layered on the Seven rather than a second doctrine. -->
    <requireOne>
      <li><li>ARIOIAF_Royalty_Exalted</li></li>
      <li><li>ARIOIAF_Lineage_Pure</li></li>
    </requireOne>

    <!-- The pride of the dragonlords, as a mild net-negative pull on generated followers. -->
    <agreeableTraits>
      <li><def>Abrasive</def></li>
      <li><def>Greedy</def></li>
    </agreeableTraits>
    <disagreeableTraits>
      <li><def>Kind</def></li>
    </disagreeableTraits>
    <randomizationSelectionWeightFactor>0</randomizationSelectionWeightFactor>
    <generalRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>memeAdjective-&gt;dragon-blooded</li>
        <li>memeAdjective-&gt;dragonborn</li>
        <li>memeConcept-&gt;ancestry</li>
        <li>memeConcept-&gt;dynasty</li>
        <li>memeConcept-&gt;the bloodline</li>
        <li>memeLeaderNoun-&gt;dragonlord</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </generalRules>
    <symbolPacks>
      <li>
        <theme>dragons</theme>
        <adjective>dragon-blooded</adjective>
        <member>dragonlord</member>
      </li>
    </symbolPacks>
    <descriptionMaker><rules><rulesStrings><li>lesson(tag=meme_ARIOIAF_BloodOfTheDragon)-&gt;the blood of the dragon follows its own traditions</li></rulesStrings></rules></descriptionMaker>
  </MemeDef>
</Defs>
